% =============================================================================
% SECTION 1: INTRODUCTION
% =============================================================================
\section{Introduction}
\label{sec:introduction}

\subsection{From Mechanism to Validation}

The v7.03 generation \citep{mutantdefi2026macrosurf} executed a single, attributable evolutionary step over the v7.02 macro-futures fleet \citep{mutantdefi2026hypersurf}: holding the model, features, and entry logic frozen, it rebuilt only the exit architecture, adding an omega-reversal exit on model state, a regime-adaptive stop on price distance, and a time-decay overlay with a stale-loss cut on holding time. In a controlled mechanism-validation backtest the cascade fired end-to-end and capped a losing trade at $-0.83\%$ against the v7.02 flat-stop realizations near $-1.5\%$.

That was a proof that the machinery \emph{works}, not a proof that it \emph{pays}. The distinction is the entire subject of this paper. v7.03 could not measure its own edge, because the instruments it traded---builder-deployed HIP-3 synthetic commodity and equity-index perpetuals---are fundamentally data-poor: the venue serves only three to four days of one-minute history for each, and nothing at all before June~10, 2026 for the newly listed equity-index market. The v7.03 paper was candid about this: it reported the v7.02 forward-walk as the empirical baseline and marked full walk-forward validation as \emph{pending}.

\subsection{The Real Bottleneck is Validation Capacity}

The lesson of the v7.03 cycle is epistemic, not mechanical. The library did not run out of good mechanisms; it ran out of \emph{ground on which to test them}. The clearest symptom was the equity-index leg: a candidate strategy that was fully built, fully wired, and \emph{nearly shipped}---and was retired only because a manual data-availability check happened to catch that it had three days of history. That the safeguard was manual is the problem. A library whose governing virtue is attributability (\cref{def:single-step}) must not be one keystroke away from deploying an unvalidatable strategy.

We therefore reject the tempting framing of v7.04 as ``crypto plus a list of model and feature improvements.'' That framing---funding-aware targets, ensemble models, multi-timeframe gates, asymmetric exit calibration, all at once---mutates every compositional interface simultaneously and so produces a result from which \emph{nothing can be attributed}. It is, by the library's own definition (\cref{def:single-step}), not an evolution but a rewrite. The disciplined move is the opposite: change one thing, and change the one thing that unblocks measurement.

\subsection{Contribution Summary}

This paper contributes:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item A \textbf{validation interface} $\Vset$ (\cref{sec:interfaces}), promoting the choice of validation substrate from an implicit, manually checked afterthought to a first-class seam of the compositional system, and a \textbf{data-sufficiency precondition} (\cref{def:data-sufficiency}) that gates every $\{\Mset,\Fset,\Eset,\Xset\}$ mutation behind certified substrate depth---making the v7.03 index near-miss structurally impossible.
    \item A \textbf{pure substrate mutation} (\cref{sec:single-step}): \cryptosurf{} v7.04 reverts the universe to the liquid crypto leg (BTC, ETH) as a $\Pset$-only single evolutionary step, freezing $\Mset,\Fset,\Eset,\Xset$ verbatim so that the deep crypto history delivers the \textbf{first attributable edge measurement} of the v7.03 exit cascade (\cref{sec:measurement}).
    \item A \textbf{self-falsification telemetry contract} (\cref{sec:measurement}): per-exit-reason profit attribution (\texttt{omega\_reversal} vs.\ custom stop vs.\ \texttt{stale\_loss\_cut} vs.\ ROI) routed through the existing \hermes{} atomic-snapshot interface, so the library observes which of its three left-tail bounds actually pays.
    \item A \textbf{reinforcement-learning roadmap for v7.05} (\cref{sec:v705}): a full-mechanism specification for restoring \texttt{MutantReinforcementLearner} at the model interface, demonstrating that its five-action reward function encodes \emph{declaratively} the duration-and-left-tail objective v7.03 hand-coded, and that it is gated precisely by the substrate v7.04 establishes.
\end{enumerate}

% =============================================================================
% SECTION 2: THE LIBRARY AS A SET OF INTERFACES
% =============================================================================
\section{The Library as a Set of Interfaces}
\label{sec:interfaces}

\subsection{The Compositional System and the Single-Step Discipline}

The library is a compositional system whose components meet at stable interfaces. We restate the v7.03 formalism and the discipline it imposes.

\begin{definition}[Compositional Trading System]
\label{def:system}
A \emph{compositional trading system} is the tuple $\mathcal{T}=(\Mset,\Fset,\Eset,\Xset,\Pset)$ where $\Mset$ is the predictive \textbf{model}, $\Fset$ the \textbf{feature} pipeline, $\Eset$ the \textbf{entry} generator, $\Xset$ the \textbf{exit} architecture, and $\Pset$ the \textbf{portfolio} (the tradeable universe and cross-asset legs). Each component is realized at a concrete code seam, summarized in \cref{tab:interfaces}.
\end{definition}

\begin{definition}[Single Evolutionary Step]
\label{def:single-step}
A \emph{single evolutionary step} is a transformation $\mathcal{T}\to\mathcal{T}'$ that modifies exactly one component of $\mathcal{T}$ while holding the others invariant. Such a step is \emph{attributable}: any change in realized performance is causally restricted to the single mutated interface. A transformation that mutates two or more components simultaneously is a \emph{rewrite} and is, by construction, unattributable.
\end{definition}

\begin{remark}[A sharpening of the v7.03 definition]
v7.03 defined the single step permissively, as a change to ``at most $(\Xset,\Pset)$.'' The v7.03 cycle itself shows why that permission is dangerous: it bundled an exit rebuild ($\Xset$) with a universe change ($\Pset$), so the realized improvement could not be cleanly assigned to either. \Cref{def:single-step} tightens the rule to \emph{exactly one} component. v7.04 is the first generation to honor the strict form: it touches $\Pset$ and nothing else.
\end{remark}

\begin{table}[H]
\centering
\caption{The compositional interfaces and their concrete code seams in the library.}
\label{tab:interfaces}
\small
\begin{tabularx}{\textwidth}{@{}llX@{}}
\toprule
\textbf{Interface} & \textbf{Symbol} & \textbf{Concrete seam} \\
\midrule
Model    & $\Mset$ & \texttt{SVRSurfModel.fit} (FreqAI \texttt{BaseRegressionModel}); target \verb|&-omega_return| \\
Features & $\Fset$ & \texttt{feature\_engineering\_*}, surf-kinematics + chop regime (\texttt{macro\_surf\_shared}) \\
Entry    & $\Eset$ & \texttt{populate\_entry\_trend}; omega-gated competitive scoring, \texttt{quality\_threshold} \\
Exit     & $\Xset$ & \texttt{populate\_exit\_trend} + \texttt{custom\_stoploss} + \texttt{custom\_exit} (the v7.03 cascade) \\
Portfolio& $\Pset$ & \texttt{pair\_whitelist}, \texttt{macro\_cross\_legs}, \texttt{profile\_for\_pair} \\
\midrule
\textbf{Validation} & $\bm{\Vset}$ & \textbf{(new in v7.04)} substrate-depth certification + walk-forward protocol \\
Observability & --- & \texttt{DfyHermesIntelMixin} + \texttt{dfy\_snapshot\_io} (atomic JSON, MRO-first) \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabularx}
\end{table}

\subsection{The Missing Interface: Validation}

Six interfaces appear in \cref{tab:interfaces}, but only five were ever \emph{managed}. The sixth, validation, existed as an unmanaged precondition: every generation implicitly assumed its substrate carried enough history to test on, and that assumption was checked, when it was checked at all, by hand. The v7.03 index near-miss is what an unmanaged interface looks like in production.

\begin{definition}[Validation Interface]
\label{def:validation-interface}
The \emph{validation interface} $\Vset$ is the pair $(\mathcal{S},\Pi)$ where $\mathcal{S}$ is the \textbf{substrate}---the set of instruments together with the depth and continuity of their available history---and $\Pi$ is the \textbf{protocol}: the walk-forward scheme, the per-exit-reason attribution, and the falsification criteria under which a claim about $\mathcal{T}$ is admitted as evidence.
\end{definition}

\begin{definition}[Data-Sufficiency Precondition]
\label{def:data-sufficiency}
