\begin{spacing}{1.0}
\noindent\small
We present \macrosurf{} v7.03, a single, disciplined evolutionary step over the v7.02 macro perpetual-futures fleet that targets one diagnosed pathology: a structurally asymmetric payoff in which a high signal win-rate was overwhelmed by a small number of large, slow-bleeding losses. Forward-walk dry-run telemetry over June 3--12, 2026 showed realized stop-outs of $-1.46\%$ (silver) and $-1.58\%$ (gold, with an average hold of $\approx 12.6$ hours) against ROI-capped wins of only $+0.37\%$---an approximately $1{:}4$ left-tail asymmetry that rendered the metals legs omega-negative despite favorable hit-rates.

Consistent with the Omega Risk Budgeting thesis established in prior work---\emph{compress the left tail rather than chase larger wins}---v7.03 introduces three exit-side mechanisms while leaving the SVR-RBF omega-prediction model and the v7.02 entry pipeline unchanged: (1)~an \textbf{omega-reversal exit signal} that closes a position when the support-vector regression prediction flips against it with $z$-score confirmation; (2)~a \textbf{regime-adaptive custom stoploss} whose width is conditioned on the measured chop regime, cutting fastest in the light-chop conditions characteristic of metals; and (3)~a \textbf{time-decay overlay} with a hard stale-loss cut that force-tightens slow bleeders, directly capping the multi-hour drawdowns the flat stop previously permitted. The fleet is simultaneously re-weighted: the omega-negative metals legs are removed, the omega-positive energy legs are retained, and a candidate equity-index leg (XYZ-SP500) is \emph{evaluated and retired}---the venue serves only $\approx 3$ days of history for that newly-listed HIP-3 synthetic perp (nothing before June~10, 2026), too little to validate or trade. We identify the crypto leg, where BTC and ETH carry continuous liquid one-minute history, as the next omega frontier and defer it to a separate evolution (v7.04).

In a controlled mechanism-validation backtest the new exit stack fires end-to-end, capping a losing trade at $-0.83\%$ versus the v7.02 flat-stop realizations near $-1.5\%$. We report the v7.02 forward-walk as the empirical baseline and mark full v7.03 walk-forward validation as pending a multi-week dry-run of the energy fleet. The system additionally exposes a real-time intelligence feed (\hermes{}) consumed by the \mutantdefi{} front-end and an x402 payments surface.
