The asymmetry in \cref{tab:v702-asymmetry} is the entire subject of this paper. A strategy with win probability $p$, average win $w>0$, and average loss $\ell>0$ has expectancy
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:expectancy}
\mathbb{E}[\text{PnL}] = p\,w - (1-p)\,\ell .
\end{equation}
With $w \approx 0.37\%$ fixed by the ROI ladder and $\ell \approx 1.5\%$ fixed by the flat stop, the break-even win-rate is $p^\star = \ell/(w+\ell) \approx 0.80$. A signal that is right $75\%$ of the time still loses money. The corrective lever is not $p$ (entry quality) but $\ell$ (loss magnitude). This is precisely the \emph{loss-compression} prescription of the Omega Risk Budgeting program \citep{mutantdefi2025volatility,mutantdefi2025omegabudget}.

\subsection{Contribution Summary}

v7.03 contributes:

\begin{enumerate}
    \item An \textbf{omega-reversal exit} (\cref{sec:omega-exit}) that converts the frozen SVR prediction into a closing signal, so a position is abandoned when the model's directional conviction reverses with $z$-confirmation---bounding $\ell$ from the signal side.
    \item A \textbf{regime-adaptive custom stoploss} (\cref{sec:adaptive-stop}) that replaces the flat $-1.2\%$ with a chop-conditioned width, tightest in the light-chop regime that dominated the metals draw-downs.
    \item A \textbf{time-decay overlay and stale-loss cut} (\cref{sec:time-decay}) that force-tighten and ultimately evict slow bleeders, directly attacking the $\approx 12.6$\,h gold holds.
    \item A \textbf{fleet re-weighting} (\cref{sec:fleet}): metals removed as proven omega-negative, a candidate equity-index leg evaluated and retired on a data-availability constraint, energy retained, and data-gated cross-asset informative legs (\enquote{where data supports}).
    \item A \textbf{real-time intelligence feed} (\cref{sec:hermes}), \hermes{}, that publishes open-trade and indicator snapshots to the \mutantdefi{} front-end and an x402 payments surface via an atomic JSON contract.
\end{enumerate}

\begin{definition}[Single Evolutionary Step]
\label{def:single-step}
Given a compositional system $\mathcal{T}=(M,\mathcal{F},\mathcal{E},\mathcal{X},\mathcal{P})$, a \emph{single evolutionary step} is a transformation $\mathcal{T}\to\mathcal{T}'$ that modifies at most the exit architecture $\mathcal{X}$ and the portfolio/universe $\mathcal{P}$, while holding the model $M$, feature pipeline $\mathcal{F}$, and entry generator $\mathcal{E}$ invariant. Such a step is \emph{attributable}: any change in realized performance is causally restricted to $(\mathcal{X},\mathcal{P})$.
\end{definition}

