\section{The Preserved Substrate}
\label{sec:substrate}

To make \cref{def:single-step} concrete we first fix what does \emph{not} change.

\subsection{Omega-Style Regression Target}

The model remains \texttt{SVRSurfModel}, an $\varepsilon$-insensitive support-vector regressor with a radial-basis kernel \citep{vapnik1995nature,scholkopf2002learning}, wrapped in \texttt{MultiOutputRegressor} for multi-target operation. Its label is the volatility-normalized forward return
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:omega-target}
\&\text{-omega\_return}_t \;=\; \frac{r^{\text{fwd}}_{t,h}}{\sigma^{\text{bwd}}_{t,k}+\epsilon},
\qquad
r^{\text{fwd}}_{t,h}=\frac{C_{t+h}}{C_t}-1,
\end{equation}
with forward horizon $h$ equal to \texttt{label\_period\_candles}~$=30$ and $\sigma^{\text{bwd}}$ the trailing realized volatility. This target is an \emph{omega proxy}: it rewards predicted upside per unit of recent downside variability, aligning the regression objective with the Keating--Shadwick omega ratio \citep{keating2002universal} rather than with raw return. The trained prediction is denoted $\omegahat_t \equiv \&\text{-omega\_return}_t$ in the analyzed dataframe, with a standardized companion $z_t \equiv \texttt{freqai\_z}$.

\subsection{Entry Pipeline (Frozen)}

The entry generator $\mathcal{E}$---surf-kinematics features, chop-regime classification, spanning-extrema detection, quality scoring, and competitive selection---is inherited verbatim from the v7.02 mixin. Entries continue to fire on $\omegahat_t > \tau_\omega$ with $z$-confirmation and the v7.02 quality gates; the enter tag \texttt{macro\_v702\_long} is preserved precisely so that exit-attribution studies can join v7.02 and v7.03 trades on a common entry definition.

